p(15,18,"it was fully settled that James should go to Clifford Hall",
 "It is settled that James will go to Clifford Hall in a month or six weeks, and meanwhile he gets driving practice. The carriage goes out more often, and James drives.",
 "A few days after this talk it was all decided that James would go to Clifford Hall in a month or six weeks, as it suited his master. In the meantime he was to get all the practice in driving that he could. I had never known the carriage to go out so often before. When the mistress did not go out, the master drove himself in the chaise with two wheels. But now, whether it was the master or the young ladies, or only a small job for someone, Ginger and I were put in the carriage and James drove us. At first John rode on the box with him and told him this and that, and after that James drove alone.",
 ["settled","chaise","errand","box"])
s(15,"I would rather have them in charge with him than with half",
 "I would prefer to leave the horses with him than with half the young men I know.",
 "'would rather ... than ...' says what someone prefers; here 'in charge with him' means he has the care of them.")
