p(16,2,"After this it was decided by my master and mistress to pay a visit",
 "On the journey James drives carefully. He uses the brake going downhill, keeps the horses on smooth ground and gives them a rest on long hills.",
 "After this the master and mistress decided to visit some friends who lived about forty-six miles from home, and James was to drive them. On the first day they traveled thirty-two miles. There were some long, heavy hills, but James drove so carefully and thoughtfully that the horses were not tired out. He never forgot to put on the brake going downhill or to take it off at the right place. He kept their feet on the smoothest part of the road. If the hill going up was very long, he put the wheels of the carriage a little across the road so that it would not run back, and he gave the horses a rest to get their breath. All these little things help a horse very much, especially if he gets kind words as well.",
 ["harassed","brake","downhill","smoothest","uphill","breathing","bargain"])
s(16,"Practice makes perfect,” said the crooked little hostler, “and ’twould be a pity if it didn’t",
 "If you practice, you get perfect; and it would be sad if you did not, after forty years.",
 "’twould is the old short form of 'it would'; 'if it didn’t' stops short for 'if it didn’t make perfect'.") if False else None
s(16,"I never was cleaned so lightly and quickly as by that little old man",
 "No one ever cleaned me so lightly and so quickly as that little old man did.",
 "'never ... so lightly and quickly as ...' compares two things as equal in the negative; 'was cleaned' is the passive, with 'by that little old man' naming who did it.")
